   "body": "/claim cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet\n\nQueued after #1206 (PR #1208, in review), on cloud/orch's instruction. Plan, test first at every step:\n1. **Pure rule** (`PullRefreshRule`): pull distance → icon scale (0…1 over a named threshold constant, 72 pt as `ReaderPullWatcher.threshold`), and a per-pull tracker: it reports the full-size crossing exactly once (haptic, then the refresh), a release below the threshold does nothing, a new pull starts after the offset returns to rest. Unit tests first.\n2. **Reader**: remove the end-of-page hint (`offersPullToRefresh`, `.pull-hint`, the model flag, the tests that pin it: #820/#932), and build the growing icon and the haptic on the existing `ReaderPullWatcher` (no second mechanism); the refresh keeps the reading position (`ReaderRefresh.run` path). Check and state what the top/bottom pulls do in the `WKWebView` today.\n3. **Lists** (topic lists first, then the MP list): top and bottom pull on `onScrollGeometryChange` with the same rule and `arrow.clockwise`; Reduce Motion: no growth animation; VoiceOver keeps an accessibility action to refresh.\n4. Legacy @ 87fe0d1c: cite what it does at the ends of a list and of the reader (no guess), ledger `gap-edit`/`gap-new`, draft PR with `compile-check`, Opus review, ready line on #893.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
